---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { ui } from "../../i18n/ui";

const mail = "info@wohnentscheid-frankfurt.de";
---
<Base lang="en" title={ui.en.titles.privacy}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This is a translation. The German version is legally binding: <a href="/datenschutz/" hreflang="de" lang="de">Datenschutz</a>.</p>

    <h2>In short</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies. It has no tracking and no statistics. It loads nothing from other servers.
      Fonts and images are on our own server.
    </p>

    <h2>Responsible</h2>
    <address>
      Sven Nagel<br />
      Ostendstraße 9<br />
      60314&nbsp;Frankfurt am Main<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>
    </address>

    <h2>Server and log</h2>
    <p>
      The website is on a server of Hetzner Online GmbH in Nuremberg. Hetzner processes the data on our behalf.
      The connection is encrypted with HTTPS.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each time you open a page, the server writes an entry in the log: time, page, type of request, answer of the
      server, amount of data, duration and a shortened IP address. The server shortens the IP address before it
      saves it. For IPv4 the first two of four parts stay, for IPv6 the first 32 bits. We do not save your browser
      or the page you came from.
    </p>
    <p>
      We need the log to find errors and attacks. The legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate
      interest is a safe operation. The server deletes the entries after seven days at the latest.
    </p>

    <h2>Map “Sozialraum Frankfurt”</h2>
    <p>
      At wohnentscheid-frankfurt.de/sozialraum-frankfurt/ we show a map. The background map comes from basemap.de.
      This is a service of the Federal Agency for Cartography and Geodesy (Bundesamt für Kartographie und Geodäsie,
      BKG). Your browser loads the tiles of the background map from our server. Our server fetches them from the
      BKG. The BKG only sees our server. It gets neither your IP address nor details about your browser. We do not
      write the tile requests to the log.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to us, we process your address and your message. We use them only to answer you. Our mailbox is
      at IONOS SE in Montabaur. The legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is to answer
      your questions. We delete your email when we no longer need it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      You can sign up with the form on our website. Then we send you an email with a link. We add you only when you
      confirm there. This way nobody can sign up another person's address. For the form, our server at Hetzner
      processes your address and your IP address. It does not save them. To block misuse, it keeps them in memory
      for 24 hours at most. We send the emails through IONOS.
    </p>
    <p>
      After you confirm, we get an email with your address. It also says if you signed up on the German or the
      English page. We save your address, your topics and the date you signed up. We use them to send you our
      newsletter now and then. We do not measure if you open it or click on links. The legal basis is your consent
      according to Art.&nbsp;6(1)(a) GDPR. We keep the data until you unsubscribe. For blocking misuse, the legal
      basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is to protect the form against misuse.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can unsubscribe at any time: with the link in every email or with an email to us. After you unsubscribe,
      we keep your address with the note “unsubscribed”. This way you do not get mail from us again by mistake.
      The legal basis for this is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>Signal, Instagram and GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      We link to our Signal group, our Instagram profile and our GitHub account. These are simple links. You leave
      our website only when you click. Then the privacy rules of Signal, Instagram or GitHub apply. In the Signal
      group, the other members
      see your Signal name.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correction, deletion and restriction of processing. You have the right to data
      portability (Art.&nbsp;15 to 20 GDPR). You can withdraw your consent at any time for the future. To do so,
      write to <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Objection:</strong> Where we rely on Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR, you can object at any time
      (Art.&nbsp;21 GDPR). An email to us is enough.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a supervisory authority. The authority for us is the Hessian Commissioner for Data
      Protection and Freedom of Information (Der Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit),
      Gustav-Stresemann-Ring 1, 65189&nbsp;Wiesbaden, <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de/">datenschutz.hessen.de</a>.
    </p>

    <p><small>Last updated: November 2026</small></p>
  </div>
</Base>
